<title>POLAND: Most Polish min T-bill prices rise at tender.</title>
<headline>Most Polish min T-bill prices rise at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish T-bills rose at the primary auction on total demand of 923 million zlotys against a 600 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury accepted 566 million zlotys worth of bids.  </p>
<p>			 8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    --	95.49    91.18     --	83.54</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.48)  (91.13)    --     (83.54)</p>
<p>   new max price    --	95.65    91.30     --	83.66</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.72)  (91.53)    --     (83.81)</p>
<p>   offer		--	100.0    100.0     --	400.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    --	271.5    219.5     --	431.8</p>
<p>   bids accepted    --	100.6    136.4     --	328.9</p>
<p>   next auction    100.0     --	 --	 --	400.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
